+# Calligraphy Greenway / CMP Park Lane study
+
+The user chose CMP Park Lane’s planted facade, with park space in front, as this gym’s visual anchor, and approved the generated study with “Use this direction.”
+
+The operator’s daylight exterior photo supplies the asymmetric white mass, dark bronze projecting upper window boxes, glass grids, horizontal planted bands and planted retail base. Its interior photo is material context only. Keep the white/bronze silhouette and living wall; omit logos, foreground obstructions and distant skyline. The native Station supplies rendering style only.
+
+One transparent building cutout is requested. Existing native lawns/paths will provide the front park space rather than baking a second landscape into the building image. Native size, palette, collision and placement are unallocated. Door22,36, approach22,37 and arrival22,39 remain fixed constraints.
+
+The original built-in imagegen output will be preserved unchanged under isolated project artifacts, with exact prompt and measured raster limits. A study is not a native ROM asset or an installation claim.
