+Use case: stylized-concept.
+Asset type: one original photo-referenced building cutout for a north-up Game Boy Advance / FireRed Taichung city map.
+
+The user chose CMP PARK LANE / 勤美誠品綠園道's planted facade as the architectural anchor for the Calligraphy Greenway gym, with park space in front supplied by the game map.
+
+Image1 is the building operator's actual daylight exterior photograph. Use it for architecture: an asymmetric, white modern retail/parking building; substantial white wall masses; dark bronze-brown rectangular projecting window-frame boxes high on the left and upper right; thin regular glass/window grids inside those dark boxes; long horizontal planted bands down the right frontage; and a broad dense living green wall wrapping the low retail base. Retain the offset taller left mass and the building's real stepped roof outline. The planted facade is the main recognition cue. Omit all lettering/tree logos from the white end wall. Do not make a generic symmetric museum, glasshouse, ivy-covered cottage, castle or fantasy tower.
+Image2 is the operator's INTERIOR green-wall photograph: use ONLY its plant colors and living-wall character, never copy its indoor hall, stairs, artificial lights or architecture.
+Image3 is the approved native Station sprite: use ONLY the restrained pixel rendering, frontal north-up RPG projection and modest roof-depth treatment. Do not copy station geometry, clock, red brick or spire.
+
+Create one complete centered building in a south-facing, orthographic overworld view, facade baseline horizontal, walls vertical and roof surfaces modestly visible from above. Reinterpret the real oblique photo into the game's straight frontage without a45-degree isometric rotation. Compress repetitive floors/windows into a manageable readable game silhouette while preserving the asymmetric white/bronze massing and green planted bands. Reveal a small legible ground-level glazed entry near the center of the bottom facade, with the future right central doorway cell clear. The foreground trees in the reference may be omitted to make the real planted base visible.
+
+Target logical envelope192x192 pixels (12x12 metatiles), shown as a consistent8x enlarged1536x1536 study if possible. Keep the building base at the bottom facade row, center entry around columns5–6. Use crisp economical square clusters, two or three flat material shades each, roughly15 opaque colors total: lush medium and dark green, small light-green accents, white/ivory walls, dark bronze frames and desaturated gray-blue glazing. Repeat plant/window motifs rather than photographic leaf noise. Simple daylight highlights upper left.
+
+True transparent alpha outside the building, hard binary edges. Leave the park ground in front transparent: the game will place its own existing lawn/path/tree tiles there, so the sprite contains the building only. No grass floor, pavement, park scenery, surrounding trees, skyline buildings, people, cars, shop signs, logos, text, UI, watermark, checkerboard, detached cast shadow, bloom/glow, soft alpha halo, gradients, antialiasing, painterly texture or photorealism. This is one architectural study for later native indexed conversion, not a rendered full city.
