+Use case: stylized-concept
+Asset type: transparent pixel-art overworld landmark sprite proposal for a north-up Game Boy Advance style Taichung RPG.
+Primary request: generate ONE new National Taiwan Museum of Fine Arts building sprite with one SMALL OPTIONAL DETACHED red angular sculpture sprite beside it on the same transparent canvas. This is an architecture/composition proposal, not a generic monster gym.
+Input images: Image1 official photo = reference for broad rectilinear stone museum mass and the optional red angular lawn sculpture. Image2 official photo = reference for the long dark glazed visitor frontage and thin projecting glass/metal canopy on slender supports. Images3 and4 approved Station/Miyahara studies = pixel-art rendering style ONLY; do not borrow their historic architecture, red brick, pitched roofs, arches, clock towers or grand entrance pillars.
+Subject: a broad LOW horizontal, flat-roofed museum, natural warm gray/taupe stone-clad rectilinear upper mass, a few large dark openings, continuous dark entrance/glazing band, very THIN projecting canopy with a restrained regular rhythm of slender supports. Preserve the real museum's quiet modern proportions and low mass. Stone reads as a few simple tonal groups, not photographic speckle. No grand colonnade or temple/gym silhouette.
