@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+Use case: stylized-concept
+Asset type: ONE proposed transparent north-up Game Boy Advance style park-landmark module for a Taichung RPG.
+Subject: Maple Garden / Qiuhong Valley, specifically its SUNKEN URBAN PARK identity: an asymmetric pond in a lowered basin, curved green embankments, pale winding pedestrian paths, a red-railed pedestrian bridge, and the real small modern glazed park-side pavilion shown in the references. Landscape is the primary recognition cue. The actual pavilion is secondary, never a generic gym building.
+Input image1: official Tourism pond overview, architectural/landscape reference. Preserve the depression, curved lawns and walking paths, water and modest viewing deck. Input image2: official Xitun District photo, reference for the actual low glass-fronted pavilion beneath a thin irregular angled concrete canopy with a few inclined supports, and the red-railed bridge. The city towers, crowds, advertising and logos in those photos are context and MUST NOT appear. Input image3: approved Old Station study, PIXEL RENDERING STYLE ONLY; do not borrow any station roof, tower, arches, historic ornament, red-brick facade or architecture.
+Composition: one compact integrated park module, roughly256x192 logical pixels, enlarged6x as a1536x1152 preview. Standard north-up RPG top-down three-quarter view, clear top surfaces and modest visible vertical depth, vertical pavilion facade lines remain vertical, no dramatic isometric diamond rotation. Use the pond and green banks across most of the module; put the small actual concrete/glass pavilion on the near-left/southwestern rim with its glazing facing south. The pond sits behind/right of it. A restrained red-railed bridge crosses a narrow water section, and the pale winding path descends from the outer rim into the basin. A small dark-wood viewing deck may sit on an edge only as shown in photo1. Show the SUNKEN depression with two or three shallow planted contour/shadow steps; the park is cut into ground, not raised on a floating fantasy island or a giant cliff/plinth. Provide a clear south pedestrian access opening leading toward the pavilion/path network. This composition is a compressed proposal, not a surveyed site plan.
+Architecture: low modern glass/concrete pavilion, thin slanted roof and sparse inclined supports faithful to photo2. NO Chinese/traditional pavilions, no twin Taichung Park lake pavilions, no palace/gym, no clock tower, no pagoda, no grand pillars, no invented structures. No roof signs, lettering, banners or logos.
+Style: hard square pixel clusters with deliberate stepped edges, restrained dark outlines and readable GBA-scale materials matching the style reference. Intended15 opaque colors plus transparency: a few greens for lawn/trees, blue-green water, pale path/concrete gray, dark glazing/wood and restrained red bridge accents. Mostly green foliage with small maroon planted-edge accents as photographed; NOT an orange autumn forest. Sparse simplified trees only within the park module, no scenic forest background. Daylight from upper left, matching the game city. No smooth gradients, no blur, no haze or glow, no painterly speckle and no antialiasing.
+Background: genuine transparent RGBA outside the irregular park module, strictly binary alpha0/255. Water, lawns and internal park paths are part of this landmark, but nothing outside it: no city skyline, surrounding roads, sky, horizon, crowds, people, animals, vehicles, labels, map pins, UI, border, legend or presentation board. No soft drop-shadow halo. Deliver ONE park module only, not variants or a collage.
+Implementation constraints: existing game gym entrance12,32, approach12,33 and arrival12,35 must remain unchanged for future Main fitting; do not draw coordinates or imply a final map footprint. This is only an artwork proposal. Native graphics/palette allocation and mechanical encoding are later work after review.
