+# Science Museum exhibition-entrance study
+
+The user selected the main exhibition entrance with its broad gray facade and deep central recess. The separate Botanical Garden glasshouse is excluded. The actual proposed facade artwork still needs focused review.
+
+Use the inspected official photo for the low rectangular gray masses, sparse horizontal window bands, deep entry and thin supports. Omit its temporary exhibition banner, trees, forecourt, people and distant skyline. The accepted native Station sprite supplies pixel treatment and north-up facade/roof projection only.
+
+The provisional 192×128 logical envelope would preserve door24,20 at local6,7 if placed at18,13. Root will check actual occupancy, streets, palette and bank capacity before native registration; this is not a final map-space allocation. Approach24,21 and arrival24,23 stay clear.
+
+One transparent built-in imagegen study is requested with a roughly14-color flat gray/blue-gray palette, economical repeatable modules and crisp pixels. Preserve the generated original unchanged, measure actual raster limits, and prepare deterministic indexed conversion separately after review. A large generated study is not a native game screenshot or proof of tile readiness.
