+# Shen Ji: next architecture reference brief
+
+Architecture remains open for user review. This brief prepares the choice of a recognizable village composition; no art or native changes are included.
+
+The inspected official photos show small cream two-story dormitories, red/orange gabled tile roofs, rectangular windows and weathered gray bases. Narrow pedestrian lanes, shade and small-shop adaptations distinguish the village. A second view verifies an attached exterior stair and a mural-covered gable. The tourism authority identifies the site's origin as staff housing and its later creative-shop use.
+
+At native scale, retain the two-story rhythm, roof triangles and a readable pedestrian gap. Simplify window repetitions and roof tiles. Treat umbrellas, stall shade and a stair as optional separate details; omit changing shop logos, mural artwork, strings of text and crowds from the first structural study. The current mural is reference context, not an approved permanent facade.
+
+**First focused decision:** depict a compact two-building courtyard cluster or one representative shopfront? The courtyard cluster is the recommendation for review, since it communicates a village. The user has not approved either composition; this does not reserve additional map space.
+
+The Greenway gym door stays **(10,44)**, approach **(10,45)** and arrival **(10,47)**. The current [8,41,13,44] placeholder is not a bespoke-art envelope. Keep the active gym entry distinct from any decorative shop doors.
+
+Sources and photo credit: [Taichung Tourism's official gallery](https://travel.taichung.gov.tw/zh-tw/attractions/intro/1139) and [Taichung Film Assistance's scene listing](https://filmtaichung.org.tw/scenesContent/179). Inspected image URLs/hashes are in `references-next.json`; photos are reference material only.
