+# Taichung Park Lake Heart Twin Pavilions — first study
+
+Produce one recognizable pavilion architecture cutout, independently of Miyahara,
+the Theater, the Station and the ordinary-block fill pass. The lake, shore and
+park landscaping remain separate composition inputs.
+
+The primary reference is the city's 2023 restored elevation. It shows two pointed
+concave metal roofs with thin finials and eyebrow vents, ivory splayed columns,
+brown timber glazing, a low connecting hall and a dark curved metal railing.
+Its daylight roof color is aged gray-green/gray metal. Older or nighttime photos
+are supporting shape references rather than the authority for the current color.
+
+The actual Zhongshan access bridge is red timber with straight balusters and
+spindle-like post heads. The pale arched bridge in the distant background is a
+different structure. Keep those identities separate. The generation prompt
+allows only a small subordinate timber deck stub; the full bridge and its
+collision-safe walking route belong to later composition.
+
+Match the accepted Station/Theater art family: south-facing horizontal facade,
+north-up slightly elevated GBA overworld camera, small roof depth, crisp stepped
+pixel clusters and restrained flat shading. The Station reference supplies art
+finish only. It must not transfer its clock, brick walls or roof geometry.
+
+The provisional target is 192×128 logical pixels, or12×8 metatiles, requested as
+an 8× enlarged 1536×1024 transparent PNG. The existing pilot offers a larger 16×12
+art envelope. These are sizing inputs, not accepted native tile/collision data.
+No native palette bank or global graphics budget is allocated by this study.
+
+One first built-in `image_gen` call produced `park-study-v1.png`. No postprocessing
+was applied; the original RGBA bytes and transparency are preserved. The exact
+prompt is `generation-prompt-v1.txt`; input identities and hashes are in
+`references.json`, and output/hash/raster measurements are in `generation.json`.
+
+The first output preserves the main architectural identity. Its alpha is soft,
+its raster is not an exact enlarged logical grid, and the tiny red deck stub
+reads as a barrier across the entry. Those observations remain true of the
+unchanged generated study. The separate mechanical candidate now has binary
+alpha, the exact Station palette and validated packed-file round trips, as
+recorded in `candidate-notes.md`. Keep `nativeReady=false`: composition must
+still open the approach, merge the shared graphics budget, supply actual ground
+and collision, bind the door/returns and prove runtime behavior.
+
+The sole first review decision concerns recognizable twin-pavilion identity.
+The actual PNG was delivered immediately, before completing the metadata pack.
+The user approved the direction with “Use this direction.” Source art is frozen.
+One authorized mechanical native candidate is now prepared; Root's combined-bank
+audit and functional portal composition remain independent integration work.
