index 0000000..dbc402b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/data/taichung/oldcity-buildings/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+# OldCity city-v3 buildings
+
+Codex's approved city-v3 building study (`data/taichung/neighborhoods/city-v3-studies`)
+converted to native art and installed into OldCity's generic apartment blocks.
+
+- `art/`: all eight study buildings as indexed PNGs in the OldCore Taichung kit palette
+  (secondary slot 12). Made by `tools/taichung/streetscape/oldcity_buildings_art.py`.
+- `placements.json`: the replaced blocks, 19 buildings and the trees and hedges in
+  leftover rows.
+- `install.json`: what `tools/taichung/streetscape/oldcity_buildings.py` installed.
+  Run it with `--check` to require the working tree to match a fresh install.
+
+OldCity uses three styles: townhouse, teal duplex and balcony walk-up. The install is
+additive, so every existing OldCore definition, graphic and palette stays as it is, and
+three styles are what fit:
+
+- 85 free secondary metatile IDs (the three styles need 72);
+- 118 free graphics (their tiles are merged from 210 to fit).
+
+The other five styles are converted but unmerged, ready for a bank with more room.
+
+Each replaced cell keeps its collision and elevation. Both connection strips stay
+byte-identical, including Greenway's view of OldCity x0-7 on rows 0-62. Save version 8
+refreshes a saved OldCity map cache on Continue; no position moves.
