+
+Both plans preserve exact connected-strip entry words, graphics, palette RGB and attributes. Equal RGB alone is insufficient because camera transitions retain tilemap entries that still reference raw graphics. The current engine reloads only secondary banks on a camera connection. The one-function conditional full-primary reload proposal remains an **unapplied artifact patch**; asynchronous DMA ordering, weather/tint, General animation restart, heap/task pressure, native walking/biking seams and Continue require independent acceptance before private primaries can ship. Main owns saved-scene versioning and exact relocation policy. No current release should include a private primary merely because these static capacity simulations pass.
+
+## Reproduction
+
+Use the project's Python3.11/Pillow interpreter. Each leaf has its own encoder and saved-byte validation. CMP's default encoder requires the checked palette proposal; regenerate that proposal with `prepare_palette.py` first. Generated `.4bpp` and `.gbapal` files follow the repository's normal ignore rules and can be reproduced from the tracked indexed PNG/palette and encoder.
