+# Gym interiors and the Wanhe Temple gym (save v12)
+
+Approved by the user on 2026-11-11 from the gym interiors review board (draft 3; the Park room from draft 4, option B). Base: native `9cb6855` (the guest house opening).
+
+## What changed
+
+- **Every gym has its own room** that follows its building's shape: `LAYOUT_TAICHUNG_GYM_*` in `data/layouts/TaichungGym*/`.
+  Four rooms reuse a FireRed tileset pair as they are (Science Museum, Greenway, Shen Ji, Wanhe Temple); the other six
+  (Old Station, Park, Miyahara, Fine Arts, Fengjia, Theater) each get a private secondary tileset
+  `data/tilesets/secondary/taichung_gym_*` (at most 384 tiles and metatiles, palettes 7-12) that mixes FireRed pieces with new art.
+- **Each room keeps only its two existing people**, the leader and one helper, with their existing scripts and text. Only where they stand changed.
+- **Exits.** Warp 1 is the middle exit mat (`MB_SOUTH_ARROW_WARP`), the cell every outside door targets. Warps 0 and 2 are
+  landing cells beside it (`install_gyms.exit_warps` falls back to the two cells above the mat if a room ever lacks open floor beside it).
+- **Taichung Park is on dry ground.** The pavilion stands on the lakeshore outside (plaza and street to the south, lake to the north),
+  so its room has no water: one open tea hall under both roofs, tea tables in the wings, a red runner from the door to Lian, and the
+  lake seen only through the north windows. An earlier lake-pavilion version with water all round and a bridge was replaced on the
+  user's request.
+- **Muqing's gym moved to Wanhe Temple.** She keeps save bit 8 (`TAICHUNG_GYM_MAPLE_GARDEN`, ID `maple-garden`) and her team,
+  and her lines now speak of Mazu and the sea; her badge is the Tide Badge / 潮汐徽章 (same water-drop art). In the temple she gives no
+  history tour, because the temple host beside her tells Wanhe's story. Maple Garden became a visit-only hall: its scientist guide
+  stands where the leader stood and the room plays `MUS_FUCHSIA`. The city contract marks Wanhe as a gym and Maple Garden as a
+  `landmark-hall`, and the minimap contract follows (`export_minimap.py`).
+- **Save v12.** A save made inside any of the eleven rooms (ten gyms plus Maple Garden) by an older version reloads that room on
+  its exit mat (warp 1). A pending explicit target inside a room is repaired the same way; a native door return keeps its own arrival.
+  Nothing else changes: the version is the only other byte written.
+  The older suite (`tests/taichung_save_test.c`) expects that reload wherever its cases sit in a gym room.
+
+## Rebuilding and checking
+
+    cd tools/taichung/gym_interiors && python3 -B install_gyms.py   # re-derives every room, tileset, map and layout entry
+    python3 -B tools/taichung/gym_interiors/verify_gyms.py .        # people on floor, reachable from the exit mat
+    python3 -B tools/taichung/gym_interiors_guard.py --self-test    # the registered layer guard
+    python3 -B tools/taichung_gameplay/test-save-v12.py             # save v12 host cases
+
+`install_gyms.py` reproduces the installed files byte for byte. `tools/taichung/gym_interiors_guard.py` pins every edited and added file,
+ships the base copies of edited files in `data/taichung/gym-interiors/baseline`, and offers `underneath()` so older guards read the
+tree beneath this layer; `home_start.py` peels it first, so every guard that peels the guest house layer also sees beneath this one.
+
+After editing a pinned file, or merging another change over this layer, re-pin with `gym_interiors_guard.py --install`. It refreshes
+the files the manifest already lists, so a merged change's own files stay out of this layer. `--install --rescan` takes the list from
+git against `9cb6855` instead, whether the layer is committed or not, to add or drop files; on a merged tree it would also take the
+other change's files. When the git history is there, the self-test also checks that each pinned file is edited or added as git says.
+
+Runtime QA (2026-11-11, ROM built from this tree): each room loaded from a v11 save made inside it and arrived on its exit mat;
+the leader and helper each talked; the exit led to the building's door and re-entering landed on the mat; the theater's seat aisles
+(rows 6 and 8) were walked end to end with the player drawn in front of the row behind.
+ROM 056a1ca6 was walked again in Park, Wanhe Temple and Maple Garden; the dry-ground Park tea hall was walked on the ROM rebuilt after it.
