+# Landmark budget
+
+This sizes the room in each Taichung tileset for the city kit plus the eight new landmarks (13–20). `tools/taichung/kit/landmark_budget.py` measures it. The tool reads the tree, the board's master plan and the landmark plan art, and writes nothing to the tree.
+
+```sh
+python3 tools/taichung/kit/landmark_budget.py ART_DIR PLAN_JSON --measured tools/taichung/kit/landmark_measured.json \
+    --json budget.json --png landmark-budget.png
+```
+
+`ART_DIR` holds the plan art: one PNG per landmark, plus `setpieces.py` when it is present. `PLAN_JSON` is the board's `masterplan.json`. The figures below are from native `claude/city-kit` (6366b9e plus the kit) and the board art and master plan as of 9 November 2026. The JSON records each input's sha256, so a rerun shows whether the art has changed.
+
+Landmarks a district has drawn on real tiles are counted exactly, from `landmark_measured.json`. That now covers all eight:
+
+- 13–17 come from the Old City session's `tools/taichung/rework/landmark_redraw.py`: 13 and 16 at native `claude/oldcity-rework-draft` 2701bff, and 14, 15 and 17 at 7ed776a with the kit at 1f23390.
+- 18–20 come from the Nantun session's `tools/taichung/nantun/landmark_art.py` at native `claude/nantun-rework` 8628728.
+
+Every run was reproduced here.
+
+## In short
+
+- **The primaries are full.** Once the kit is in, 7 tile slots are free in all three, and all seven primary palettes are in use. Landmark art goes in each district's secondary.
+- **No existing secondary has a free palette.** Landmark art must be drawn in colours the target's palettes already hold, or a palette must be reclaimed. A new map's secondary brings six free palettes.
+- **Where each landmark fits:**
+
+| Secondary | Landmarks | Tiles needed (low–high) | Room | Verdict |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| NantunNorth | 20 | 15, drawn | 130 free, +208 reclaimable | Fits, leaving 115 |
+| GreenwayCmp | 13 | 37, drawn | 128 free, +4 reclaimable | Fits, leaving 95 |
+| Nantun (Wanhe) | 18, 19 | 51, drawn | 125 free, +46 reclaimable | Fits, leaving 74 |
+| New secondary (Old City North) | 14, 15, 17 | 95, drawn | 258 free after the carried city-v3 styles | Fits, leaving 163 |
+| OldCore | 16 | 8, drawn | 0 free, +8 reclaimable | Fits, after reclaiming |
+
+"Low" is the plan art's own detail. "High" is the detail of the landmarks shipped today. The method section below explains both.
+
+## Primaries after the kit
+
+| Primary | Maps | Tiles free |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `taichung_xitun_private` | Xitun | 26 |
+| `taichung_greenway_private` | Greenway, Nantun North, Wanhe | 36, shared by all three maps |
+| `taichung_old_core` | Old City | 44 |
+
+- Only 7 of those slots are free in all three primaries: the kit's spare slots. 357 definitions are free in all three.
+- These counts leave out the slots held for the city-v3 library and for Cut's mowed grass.
+- All seven primary palettes are in use.
+- `check_city_kit.py` pins each primary to the installer's output. Landmark art in a primary therefore means appending it to `install_city_kit.py` and re-pinning, and it can only use primary palette colours. Treat primary space as overflow.
+
+## Secondaries
+
+Each secondary has 384 tiles, 384 definitions and palettes 7–12. A planned map with no layout yet (Old City North, `NEW_DISTRICTS` in the tool) gets a new one on its sibling's primary. It starts from the sibling's palettes 7–12 and carries the sibling definitions it reuses, at the same IDs. Old City North carries OldCore's city-v3 styles for its own lots (0x3AB–0x3F2: 72 definitions, 118 tiles). Only 376 of the tiles are usable: `field_door.c` copies each door animation frame into the last 8 tile slots (0x3F8–0x3FF, `DOOR_TILE_START`), so they are never free. The categories mean:
+
+- **Drawn:** the map's own map.bin, border.bin or a script draws it.
+- **Carried:** a connected map shows the cell in its seam strip and draws it with this bank.
+- **Reclaimable:** the bank holds the art, but no map draws it.
+- **From 2b:** a phase 2b estimate (see the method section).
+
+| Secondary (map) | Tiles: drawn / carried / reclaimable / free / from 2b | Definitions free (+ reclaimable) | Palettes reclaimable | Free colour slots |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| XitunFinal (Xitun) | 358 / 0 / 8 / 10 / ~37 | 40 (+69) | 10, 11 | 7: 1, 12: 2 |
+| GreenwayCmp (Greenway) | 244 / 0 / 4 / 128 / ~0 | 137 (+4) | none | 7: 1, 10: 3, 11: 6, 12: 7 |
+| OldCore (Old City) | 368 / 0 / 8 / 0 / ~28 (0 in Old City's draft) | 35 (+76) | 9 | 8: 7, 10: 3, 11: 6 |
+| New (Old City North) | 118 (carried city-v3 styles) / 0 / 0 / 258 / 0 | 312 | 7–11 (OldCore copies; the styles keep 12) | — |
+| NantunNorth (Nantun North) | 22 / 16 / 208 / 130 / ~22 | 172 (+154) | 10, 11 | 7: 3, 8: 8, 9: 3, 12: 10 |
+| Nantun (Wanhe) | 198 / 7 / 46 / 125 / ~27 | 172 (+31) | none | 8: 2, 9: 9, 10: 3, 12: 1 |
+
+Nantun North's reclaimable tiles are mostly copies that Nantun's carry made of its neighbours' art. Its own map draws 22 tiles.
+
+## The landmarks
+
+| # | Landmark | Map | Tiles | Definitions | Colours (near an existing entry) | Tiles no existing palette draws | New palettes as drawn |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| 13 | Botanical Garden | Greenway | 37, drawn (plan estimate 111–123) | 31 | primary palette 3 | 0 | 0 |
+| 14 | Taichung Confucius Temple | Old City North | 37, drawn (plan estimate 88–274) | 42 | palette 12 | 0 | 0 |
+| 15 | Yizhong Street | Old City North | 19, drawn (plan estimate 64–253) | 23 | palette 12 | 0 | 0 |
+| 16 | Taichung Prefectural Hall | Old City | 8 + 19 in the primary, drawn (plan estimate 165–330) | 24 | palette 7 | 0 | 0 |
+| 17 | Second Market | Old City North | 39, drawn (plan estimate 115–165) | 37 | palette 12 | 0 | 0 |
+| 18 | Cultural Heritage Park | Wanhe | 30, drawn (plan estimate 116–428) | 19 | palette 12 | 0 | 0 |
+| 19 | Fengle Sculpture Park | Wanhe | 21, drawn (plan estimate 202–263) | 14 | palette 12 | 0 | 0 |
+| 20 | Wenxin Forest Park amphitheatre | Nantun North | 15, drawn (plan estimate 153–228) | 12 | palette 10 | 0 | 0 |
+
+- **All eight are drawn.** Each uses one existing palette and no new one.
+- **Why they cost a third or less of the plan estimate:** the redraws reuse whole cells (Greenway's grass and flowers; Miyahara's brick, arcade and porch), mirror repeated art, and fold flipped tiles together. They also put a reused top layer on a new ground, which costs a definition but no tile.
+
+## Where each piece can go
+
+- **20, Wenxin amphitheatre (Nantun North):** drawn, 15 tiles and 12 definitions in palette 10. That fits North's 130 free tiles, leaving 115.
+- **13, Botanical Garden (Greenway):** drawn, 37 tiles and 31 definitions, against Greenway's 128 free. That leaves 91 free plus 4 reclaimable (95) for Greenway's phase 2b fill of the new land north of row 31. Xitun still keeps its east strip to primary buildings (see below), so that room stays Greenway's.
+- **18, Cultural Heritage Park and 19, Fengle Sculpture Park (Wanhe):** drawn, 51 tiles and 33 definitions in palette 12, with Fengle's lake in the kit's still water. That fits Wanhe's 125 free tiles, leaving 74, so Wanhe needs no new secondary and no split.
+  - After its fill pass (native `claude/nantun-rework` e3b84d0), the Nantun session reports that its bank uses 148 of 384 definitions and 244 of 376 tiles. Of those tiles, 102 are kept from today's bank and 46 are new: 45 for the set pieces and 1 for a paved sign. The landmark counts are unchanged from 8628728.
+- **16, Prefectural Hall (Old City):** drawn. 8 tiles go in OldCore's 8 reclaimable slots and 19 in `old_core` primary slots only Old City uses, with 24 definitions. That leaves OldCore no tile at all, and the primary 18 Old City-only slots plus the 7 kit spares.
+- **14, 15 and 17 (Old City North):** the user approved splitting Old City. Old City North is a new map at x 80–124, y −3–48 (44×51) with its own secondary on the `old_core` primary, and 17 moved north to (98, 20)–(105, 29). The three are drawn: 95 tiles and 102 definitions, all in palette 12, sharing no tiles. The kit's pond and bridge pieces they use are primary, so they cost nothing. With the city-v3 styles carried (118 tiles, 72 definitions), the new bank keeps 163 tiles and 210 definitions free for Old City North's other blocks.
+  - OldCore itself has no free tile, and Old City's own draft (`tools/taichung/rework/oldcity_greenway_draft.py`, native `claude/oldcity-rework-draft` 315840d) finds that phase 2b frees none either: the demolished apartments' tiles are shared with kept landmark art or the city-v3 styles the new lots reuse.
+- **Palettes:** no existing secondary has a free palette, and all eight landmarks are drawn in colours their banks already hold. Old City North's bank starts from OldCore's palettes. Its landmarks are drawn in palette 12 and need no new palette, and the carried styles use only 12, so 7–11 are reclaimable.
+  - Old City can reclaim palette 9, and Nantun North palettes 10 and 11.
+  - The free colour slots above are where a missing colour or two can go.
+  - A new map's secondary brings 6 fresh palettes.
+
+## Seam strips
+
+A connected map draws the neighbour cells beside its seam with its own tilesets: 7 rows or columns, or 8 columns for an east neighbour (`preview_carry.strip()`). Nantun keeps North's first 7 rows to primary and kit pieces, and the Xitun draft now does the same on both of its seams:
+
+- **South strip, rows 57–63:** this already held only primary pieces. The stalls there are the city-v3 library's, which live in the primary.
+- **East strip, columns 33–39:** this held Shen Ji homes from Xitun's secondary (15 IDs, 48 tiles, palette 12), and Greenway's bank would have had to carry them. They are now the library's primary kiosk and stall.
+
+Old City's split follows the same rule. Its top rows (world 48–54) switch to primary kiosks, stalls and trees, and Old City North's bottom rows hold no secondary art. So the seam costs neither bank anything. Carrying copies just for the strip would have cost the same 118 tiles as the styles.
+
+If every district follows this rule in phase 2b, the carried tiles above become reclaimable too.
+
+## Method
+
+- **Secondaries:**
+  - A definition is drawn when its map's map.bin, border.bin or a `setmetatile` names it.
+  - It is carried when a connected map's strip shows it.
+  - It is held when it has any art, or when it sits in the old edge kit's reserved range `0x3E0`–`0x3FF`.
+  - Held but neither drawn nor carried counts as reclaimable. Tiles follow the definitions that use them.
+- **Phase 2b estimate:** the tiles today's maps draw only on cells that the plan repaints with the kit (its streets, highway, river, canals and lake). It is an estimate from the plan alone: streets the plan moves free more, and a district draft that reuses the art frees less (Old City's frees none).
+- **Low and high:** the lower and higher of two measures.
+  - *Plan art's detail:* the plan art cut into 8×8 tiles at 15-bit colour, with flips folded together. Transparent pixels show the ground beneath. Half-transparent pixels (shadows and planting) are laid over that ground: grass where the board shows the game's grass, paving elsewhere. The art comes from `setpieces.py`'s transparent layers.
+  - *Shipped detail:* today's landmarks draw a median of 3.5 distinct tiles per cell of landmark art, close to the maximum of 4, counting primary and secondary tiles alike. That figure times each plan's art cells gives the second measure.
+  - Definitions run from one per distinct 16×16 art cell to one per art cell.
+- **Palettes:** a tile fits an existing palette when each of its colours has an entry within OKLab distance 0.04 in one palette, primary 0–6 or secondary 7–12. Tiles that fit none are packed into new 15-colour palettes. The packing is first-fit, so the count is an upper bound.
+- **Exact counts come from the districts.** `landmark_measured.json` holds all eight, so the plan-stage figures stay only as the comparison in the landmark table. Running this tool on a district branch re-measures its bank.
