+# Optional distributed landmark history
+
+This source branch starts from tested PR9 native2c48f28 and preserves Main's inherited history WIP. It installs the exact12 Story records from handoff revision `npc-distribution-v1`; their raw SHA-256 values and the handoff hash are frozen in `docs/landmark-history-source-snapshot.json`.
+
+Displayed content per locale is12 signs,25 optional leader/temple pages and11 optional staff pages across10 helpers (48 pages,96 bilingual pages). The generated const module has68 total localized sign/tour/staff literals (34 EN/ZH pairs), plus the existing action/fallback UI literals. Source facts retain primary-source URLs, claims and limitations. `sourceFactReference`, helper proposals and role/provenance metadata are retained only in JSON and are never rendered or counted for glyph requests.
+
+The renderer validates all displayed sign/fact/NPC source IDs, shared action labels and fallback strings, exact payload hashes, page structure, all three native Latin width tables and CJK spacing. Maximum actual line is198px against198px safe width; maximum conservative encoded message is230bytes within the1000-byte bound. It reports98 missing glyphs against the released611. Main alone appends the final combined glyph union with pinned Fusion; no charmap/font/language file was edited here.
+
+Ten existing gym leaders keep direct Challenge plus optional About/Leave. Reading returns to the menu; B leaves normally. Completed gyms retain About/Leave without Challenge. Existing Wenchang/Wanhe temples offer informational About/Leave only, outside the ten-bit gym mask. Inherited greetings, AlreadyComplete and after-battle tails were retained; Main resolves overlap with its separately advanced gameplay/badge scripts.
+
+All ten helper messages use the exact latest `npcFacts`. Existing Aming/Ayan/Qiaoqiao/Mei/Boxun C handlers call a read-only fixed-ID staff getter and retain their normal lock/face/wait/release lifecycle. Quest-log replay skips their message and waits safely. New Main-owned actor labels are exactly `TaichungHistory_StaffMiyahara`, `StaffPark`, `StaffShenJi`, `StaffFineArts`, and `StaffMapleGarden` under the same prefix; each locks, faces, guards replay, buffers the selected staff text, displays it and releases. Their map placements belong to separate aade361 and are not changed here. Helpers remain available before and after victory; none starts a battle, awards progress, heals or writes saved settings.
+
+`bash tools/taichung_gameplay/test-landmark-history.sh` passes actual C buffer/getter/five-handler tests in both locales, invalid/temple IDs, pre/post-win reads and all256 protected saved variables. Its installed-script interpreter passes280 gym/temple routes and80 helper routes, including repeat reading, direct Challenge, B/Leave, completed gyms, exact helper IDs and replay. Installed EN/ZH native menu source bindings are also checked. These are host/source tests, with no emulator or actual native encoding/runtime claim.
+
+`render-landmark-history.py --write` alone replaces the generated C module; default mode checks exact bytes and writes a review report to the specified artifact directory. `docs/landmark-history-render-report.json` records the final line/source/glyph/buffer evidence. Main must merge the new actors, final dialogue union and guard bindings before ROM/native UI acceptance. No maps, Save/version/layout, taichung_language.c, glyph/font, ROM, UI or publication change was made here.
+
+Host/source logs are ignored under `build/taichung-tests/landmark-history-review/`. Main owns final integration, native build and review.
