diff --git a/docs/localization/bitmap-font.md b/docs/localization/bitmap-font.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..eb31218
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/localization/bitmap-font.md
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+# Native Traditional Chinese bitmap typography
+
+Selected source: **Fusion Pixel12px Monospaced zh_tw**, official release2026.10.25, under SIL Open Font License1.1. The compressed original BDF, exact manifest/hashes and all four upstream release license notices are bundled in `assets/fonts/fusion-pixel-12/` and `assets/fonts/taichung-native-font.json`. The generated derivative subset is called Taichung Native Bitmap12. Root distribution must include those notices beside the font/game, including the Ark Pixel, Cubic11 and Galmuri notices.
+
+This checkpoint is based on `5e503b47806ac70488afaf01cff246f70b59963b`, including onboarding's busyTEXTACK fix. All476FC19character-to-index mappings and the entire character-map file remain byte-identical. All476bitmap shapes deliberately change; advance remains12pixels and the cell remains12x14. Runtime font table size remains13,328bytes. Language/save/progress logic, runtime text renderer, translation arrays, menus, sign/script text and onboarding protocol are unchanged.
+
+The existing Noto Sans TC Medium12px binary masks were compared against threshold160Noto, Fusion12pxzh_hant/zh_tw and Ark12pxzh_hant. Both Fusion variants cover476/476required characters without clipping; Ark covers456/476and is not a complete replacement. Raising the Noto threshold removes ink but breaks thin strokes. Visual review selected the Taiwan-specific authored pixel face for clearer dense Traditional Chinese characters at the existing grid. Average ink pixels per glyph change66.59→52.21; this is descriptive, not a numeric legibility score. Width and line wrapping remain identical because every code and12pxadvance is unchanged.
+
+Offline240x160language/dialogue/sign/menu comparison proofs use the exact native glyph pixels, original Latin font pixels,15pxline pitch and208pxdialogue limit. They are explicitly labeled composite native-grid proofs, not emulator screenshots. Parent artifact bundle: `artifacts/worktrees/a83ca88d3f24/font-comparison/`. Native runtime typography acceptance is still pending an explicit UI lease at this source checkpoint.
+
+## One shared font source
+
+Both `tools/taichung_gameplay/refresh-chinese-glyphs.py` and `extend-chinese-glyphs.py` use `chinese_glyph_font.py`. The provider checks compressed and original BDF hashes, license presence, source metrics, character coverage and clipped/blank pixels. Configured bitmap generation needs only Python's standard library; it does not download anything or need Pillow. No `.notdef`, fallback face or legacyNotooverride is accepted for a configured bitmap checkout.
+
+```sh
+# Report only, or add --write to update shapes/append missing characters.
+PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 tools/taichung_gameplay/refresh-chinese-glyphs.py --game "$PWD" --artifacts /absolute/review/output
+# Append only, preserving all existing mappings AND shapes.
+PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 tools/taichung_gameplay/extend-chinese-glyphs.py --game "$PWD" --artifacts /absolute/review/output
+PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 tests/test_chinese_glyph_font.py
+```
+
+Refresh preserves every current code/index and renders every shape from the chosen source, then appends any missing characters. Append refuses a mixed-font existing table and uses the same source for new rows. Optional refresh `--corpus` contributes missing glyphs only; it never regenerates content. All normal writes are explicit `--write`; default is dry-run. Existing `parse_existing`/`extend` interfaces remain available through file-relative dynamic import without modifying `sys.path`.
+
+Main receives a separate artifact-only patch for the root `scripts/generate-chinese-font.py` entrypoint. It delegates to this native refresh pipeline and cannot reset menus, translationC, scripts or character codes. The legacy sorted/upstream-template generator must not be used. Main alone applies that root patch and integrates source/corpus changes.
+
+Host checks cover all required shapes, no clipping, source integrity, no fallback, append preserving old rows/codes, same-source future additions, and idempotent refresh without rewriting content. Native/UI proof, any final integration codebook union, release guards and publication remain Main-coordinated. Later feature branches must preserve this codebook and re-render/append using the bundled provider; never overwrite newer mappings with an older branch's font table.
