+# Maple collision save migration — v9
+
+Source-only migration on collision commit
+`88979b5f8ca5daafbce3a1fe128b27c2b15122ff`, above released native
+`6366b9e5c037647ce4d2a007efa3d3dfbedcdb48`. No ROM was built and no runtime
+Continue, UI or publication acceptance is claimed by this checkpoint.
+
+## Exact repair and cache scope
+
+Maps' committed `data/taichung/landmark-collision/delta.json` identifies exactly
+44 newly solid Maple illustration cells in Xitun, native map43:2. Each changed
+word is the old word OR0x0400. No art, metatile ID, elevation, door, connection,
+room, route or other map changed. The manifest supplies the qualified fallback
+at Xitun12,35: walkable tile0x3175, collision0, behavior0, elevation3, no actor,
+sign or warp. The native door12,32 and apron12,33 remain unchanged.
+
+The const44-row table applies only before version9, only on Xitun and only to
+explicit-coordinate targets with warpId-1. It runs after all older repairs.
+This ordering matters for the old v7 origins16,29 /16,30 /18,32: their earlier
+fallbacks17,29 /17,30 /19,32 now lie inside the44 newly solid cells and must
+then reach12,35. Source-version8 origins reach that fallback directly; older
+sources retain every earlier age gate before the final v9 repair.
+
+An existing native Continue warp keeps priority. Only its exact explicit
+coordinate target may be repaired; indexed/other warp IDs and unrelated safe
+returns remain unchanged. Without a pending warp, the migration uses actual
+saved `pos`, preserving the existing full map-load/cache refresh path.
+
+Source versions1–7 retain the established OldCity/Greenway/Xitun refreshes for
+the earlier changes. Source version8 refreshes Xitun only. OldCity, Greenway,
+Nantun and all other v8 maps keep their caches and saved positions. Version8
+is explicitly recognized as an established save, so it never falls into the
+legacy prototype/checkpoint path. Established saves change only variable40F7
+to9 plus any required pending return; party, currency/items, checkpoint,
+language, encounter preferences, City Pass, starter and onboarding stage stay
+owned by the save. Current/future versions exit without a migration.
+
+## Facing and memory
+
+The existing one-shot cache-only facing handoff is unchanged. An unchanged
+position refresh retains saved Up/Left; repairs and pending native arrivals
+use normal engine direction rules. Its map/position/warp-ID guards and session
+resets remain intact. `src/overworld.c` and the entire handoff implementation
+are byte-identical to the collision base. No new EWRAM state or save-layout
+field is introduced; the existing handoff remains constrained to8bytes.
+The new relocation table is44×4=176const ROM bytes; final machine-code size
+and ELF addresses remain Main's build output.
+
+## Executed validation
+
+- `bash tools/taichung_gameplay/test-save.sh` passes the full prior migration
+  suite and new v9 cases. The independent44-origin expectation is decoded from
+  released versus current map binaries, not copied from the C repair table.
+- Every origin is exercised at source versions1–8 as a saved field position
+  and as a pending target from another map, with native warp-ID priority.
+  All1,323 retained v8 Xitun walking positions refresh on their own tiles.
+  Historical chains, all other v8 districts/rooms, current/future exits,
+  empty parties, vanilla/prototype behavior and protected fields are covered.
+- The native-engine host harness passes155 cases, retaining the previous20
+  regressions and executing actual warp, avatar, direction, object-reset and
+  facing functions. It adds all44 field/pending repairs, older chains, v8 safe
+  Up/Left and unaffected/current-version cases. Inputs come independently from
+  Maps' committed manifest. Graphics/map-data services are host boundaries;
+  no substitute facing getter or setter is used.
+- `python3.11 -B tools/taichung_gameplay/test-save-facing.py --prove-regression`
+  passes; removing only the existing runtime hook reproduces saved North2
+  becoming South1. `git diff --check` passes.
+
+The host save model checks all600 party-record-sized plus872 inventory-sized
+protected bytes, saved object records, all256 variables and the checkpoint.
+It does not claim encrypted SRAM decoding or complete14-sector/native-Continue
+proof. Main owns the combined ROM build, a genuine v8 saved-origin Continue,
+the safe-facing smoke, current v9 Save/Continue, exact metadata/contract sync,
+and a narrowly rebound source/geometry profile. No existing guard pin or
+geometry assertion was weakened in this branch.
