+# Native onboarding contract proposal — v1
+
+Isolated source: `.worktrees/game-onboarding`, branch `codex/native-onboarding`, native base `5d6039c`, rebased onto signs-first checkpoint `d3803a8` (447-glyph prefix). No changes to the CMP release or existing field-language v1 packet are required.
+
+## Capability and ownership
+
+Add optional `onboardingBridge` metadata with version 1, size 48, an aligned EWRAM symbol address, and magic values below. The browser must validate metadata, actual packet magic/version/size/self-address and live frame counter before accessing this bounded mailbox. No browser writes to save variables, script state, coordinates, or other native RAM. Existing 32-byte language and 48-byte navigation packets retain their contracts. Absence of onboarding metadata means the old native opening remains the fallback; frontend must not assume support.
+
+Proposed symbol `gTaichungOnboardingBridge`, signature bytes `TCINTRO1` (magicA 0x4E494354, magicB 0x314F5254), little endian:
+
+| Offset | Type | Field / owner |
+|---|---|---|
+| 0x00 / 0x04 | u32/u32 | magicA / magicB, native |
+| 0x08 / 0x0A | u16/u16 | version=1 / size=48, native |
+| 0x0C | u32 | selfGbaAddress, native |
+| 0x10 | u32 | frameCounter, native; nonzero even publication seqlock, odd during native writes |
+| 0x14 | u32 | contextSequence, native; changes on every readiness/phase boundary |
+| 0x18 | u8 | phase, native |
+| 0x19 | u8 | flags, native |
+| 0x1A | u8 | activeLanguage (0/1/2), native |
+| 0x1B | u8 | result, native |
+| 0x1C | u32 | requestSequence, browser writes LAST |
+| 0x20 | u32 | ackSequence, native writes LAST |
+| 0x24 | u32 | requestedContext, browser |
+| 0x28 | u8 | command, browser |
+| 0x29 | u8 | requestedLanguage, browser |
+| 0x2A / 0x2B | u8/u8 | mapGroup / mapNum, native |
+| 0x2C / 0x2E | s16/s16 | local x / y, native |
+
+Phases: 0 inactive; 1 startup language; 2 welcome; 3 partner selection; 4 outdoor introduction; 5 bike; 6 minimap; 7 team; 8 nearby landmarks; 9 release/complete (NATIVE_TEXT while farewell is busy, READY alone after dismissal); 10 standalone language fallback. Flags: bit0 initialized/ready; bit1 accepts command now; bit2 native text/menu active. Commands: 1 APPLY_STARTUP_LANGUAGE; 2 ACK_TUTORIAL_CARD. Results: 0 none; 1 applied; 2 invalid command/value; 3 stale context; 4 not ready. Exactly one outstanding request, monotonic nonzero sequence, write payload/context then sequence, native validates stable payload and acknowledges only after applying.
+
+## Startup
+
+Frontend presents readable English / 繁體中文 cards before canvas startup, retaining selected preference. It submits command1 only when phase1 and accepts-command are both set. Native opens that bounded gate ONLY from the welcome-room script, after initialized new-game variables and before any welcome text/menu. Native applies the selected language itself, ACKs, closes gate, and resumes the script without native language multichoice. This does not relax the normal field-language bridge's safe-field guard. Only if a fresh native A/B edge is pressed after a release and a two-frame guard, the gate publishes phase10 and closes before invoking the existing standalone native language choice. Elapsed time never opens the native chooser automatically (a slow browser may show a hint). A late request gets stale-context/not-ready; browser must not silently claim success. Existing save Continue stays native-authoritative and uses the existing field bridge after safe-field readiness.
+
+Both fresh-game language routes then open the existing native exploration menu once, before welcome text and partner selection. Wild encounters and trainer sight each retain Off / Low / Normal choices; confirming or returning commits through the existing native preference setters. The language-zero map-script gate prevents this startup prompt from reopening on ordinary Continue or for demo saves, and does not overwrite their saved choices.
+
+## Outdoor tutorial without lock deadlocks
+
+Native dialogue and browser teaching cards are separate substates. Native renders a short bilingual page, waits until its text printer finishes, then exposes that topic with accepts-command set. The idle native page remains visible as the standalone teaching card; the browser may mirror it readably. After acknowledgment native closes that page and advances. Browser may show a readable card/highlight and ACK only the matching context. Native A or B also advances this explicit card-wait state for standalone play; no browser ACK is required for progress. Native scripts remain locked while teaching; the browser must NOT require an actual Bike/Team action or show a normal live minimap during that lock. The card explains controls, may show a clearly labeled tutorial preview anchored to packet coordinates, and instructs that these controls become available when the guide finishes. Browser ACK never toggles Bike, opens Team, grants Pokémon, teleports, or writes completion directly. Normal contextual controls and navigation resume after complete; real inputs are then tested.
+
+## Save/resume
+
+Reserve previously unused `VAR_0x40F6` with a distinctive opening-stage marker, initialized ONLY by NewGame. Existing saves with zero/unknown marker remain exempt, and aren't relocated or re-tutored. Stage advances after confirmed starter grant; existing grant's marker/party guard remains. Welcome-room Continue with a granted partner skips granting again, performs the authored exit, and resumes pending outdoor tutorial. Each completed tutorial topic advances the persistent stage. Completion is one-time. Old demo/presenter Continue remains unchanged. No source-wide save version bump is required: this is new-game opt-in state, not a geometry migration.
+
+Story owns EN/ZH words for welcome, partner invitation, granted partner transition, outdoor intro, Bike, map, Team, landmarks, release. Native owns stage and text selection. Interface owns cards, command validation, highlights and absence/fallback handling. Main owns build metadata integration and final Vercel acceptance. This draft is intentionally published before implementation; offsets and enum names will be frozen in the header and host tests next.
+
+Exact phase binding is supplied by the requestedContext: a new nonzero context is published on every phase/readiness boundary, with context zero during publication. Readers bracket all twelve words with frameCounter/context and reject zero, odd, or changed frameCounter, and zero/changed context. Every native-field write (including result/ACK) is inside an odd/even publication transaction. Requests double-read sequence/context/command/language; native retains the validated sequence through the action and publishes that exact ACK, never whichever request happens to be current afterward. Pauses and stale cards must revalidate context before ACK.
+
+## Implementation and regression notes
+
+The new flow omits the previous pre-welcome encounter-settings screen. Existing unset preferences still resolve to Normal/Normal, and their zero values are not rewritten. Existing Off/Low/Normal choices remain unchanged. Exploration settings remain optional in the normal native menu.
+
+A narrow opt-in check before ordinary field input launches the outdoor script only for this new game's pending stages in Old City. It returns immediately during quest-log playback, so recap callbacks cannot be starved by a repeating on-frame script. It does not introduce a new temp-variable write into existing saves, alter the old frame table, or script any guide/player walk.
+
+After300 native callback frames waiting for startup language, a short standalone fallback hint may appear. This is only a cue, never an automatic chooser. Phase1 may include NATIVE_TEXT while that hint prints while still accepting its bounded language command. Tutorialcard contexts remain READY+ACCEPTS_COMMAND and not NATIVE_TEXT.
+
+Story release staging: persistent A109 is pending farewell; distinct A1FF is completed. Continue at A109 resumes only farewell, then commits A1FF after dismissal. Old zero/unknown markers and completed A1FF remain exempt. This changes no mailbox offsets or command semantics.
