+## 14. Taichung Confucius Temple / 臺中孔廟 (official: Taichung City Confucius Temple / 臺中市孔廟)
+
+Verdict: verified. Song style, the Lingxing gate and the double-eaved hip roof are all confirmed by the temple's own management office. One government source disagrees on the roof type (below).
+
+- [Taichung Tourism: Taichung City Confucius Temple (en)](https://travel.taichung.gov.tw/en/attractions/intro/1371) and [臺中市孔廟 (zh)](https://taichung.travel/zh-tw/attractions/intro/41): a Song dynasty palace-style complex. Planners chose that style to set it apart from the Qing-style Martyrs' Shrine next door. The plan is a scaled-down Qufu temple, and all painted decoration is in Song style.
+- The [management office (臺中市孔廟忠烈祠聯合管理所)](https://www.confucius.taichung.gov.tw/) runs its own site. Pages used:
+  - [Architecture overview](https://www.confucius.taichung.gov.tw/837602/post): the site was an air-force children's school until 1967. It was designed and supervised by the provincial public works bureau and is built in reinforced concrete. Site area is 23,653 m². Elements: two pailou, a screen wall, the Lingxing gate, the Pan pond forecourt, the Guande and Yucui gates, the Dacheng gate, the Dacheng hall, the east and west cloisters, and the Chongsheng shrine.
+  - [欞星門](https://www.confucius.taichung.gov.tw/837653/post): the first gate, 11.95 m high and 6.6 m wide. It follows the Song 烏頭門 type, an open post-and-lintel gateway. Its columns are ceremonial pillars, its doors are lattice/fence leaves, and a pair of lions sits on the column tops. Smaller 金聲 and 玉振 gates stand on each side, joined to it by short walls. The base is grey chiselled cement and the columns are white chiselled cement. It is normally kept shut, and visitors enter by the Guande gate on Shuangshi Road ([visitor map page](https://www.confucius.taichung.gov.tw/834557/834568/834569/834585/837895/post)).
+  - [泮池](https://www.confucius.taichung.gov.tw/837655/post): a half-moon pond inside the Lingxing gate, 30 m wide, with an arched bridge (碧水橋) across the middle.
+  - [大成門](https://www.confucius.taichung.gov.tw/837661/post): a five-bay gate with a single-eaved hip-and-gable roof (歇山). Its doors are red-lacquered and studded with bronze nails.
+  - [大成殿](https://www.confucius.taichung.gov.tw/837663/post) and [其他](https://www.confucius.taichung.gov.tw/837667/post): the main hall stands in the inner court. It is 27 m wide, 19 m deep, 17.53 m tall and seven bays across. Its roof is a northern Song-imitation double-eaved hip roof (重檐廡殿) in yellow glazed tile, with no ridge beasts on the hips. The porch columns are lacquered vermilion. Eaves, brackets, beams and ceiling carry Song-style painting, mainly muted blue-green with brown beams. In front is a balustraded dance terrace with a carved central stair. The east and west cloisters (廡, 68.5 m long, roll-ridge roofs) link the Dacheng gate to the Chongsheng shrine behind the hall, closing the court on all four sides.
+  - [觀德門、毓粹門](https://www.confucius.taichung.gov.tw/837665/post) and [照壁、牌坊](https://www.confucius.taichung.gov.tw/837651/post): the side gates are hip-and-gable with 青 glazed tile. The two five-bay pailou on Lixing Road (13.4 m tall) and the screen wall outside the enclosing wall are faux-granite with 青 glazed tile. 青 here could mean green or blue-green.
+- [Taiwan Tourism Administration: 臺中孔廟](https://www.taiwan.net.tw/m1.aspx?sNo=0001016&id=10351): this is where the shorter name 臺中孔廟 comes from. It says the temple stands beside the Martyrs' Shrine at Shuangshi and Lixing Roads, with two white pailou in front and the half-moon pond and bridge behind the gate. It calls the main hall roof double-eaved hip-and-gable (歇山重簷). That contradicts the temple office's 重檐廡殿, and the operator's page is preferred.
+- Names: the tourism bureau and the temple office use 臺中市孔廟 / Taichung City Confucius Temple. The Taiwan Tourism Administration uses 臺中孔廟.
+- Address: No. 30, Section 2, Shuangshi Road, North District.
+- Coordinates: latitude `24.15432`, longitude `120.68997`, from the tourism metadata. The Taiwan Tourism Administration gives longitude/latitude `120.68995 / 24.154329`.
+- Plan note check:
+  - "Song-style hall": supported.
+  - "Behind the Lingxing gate": supported, with a refinement. The Lingxing gate is an open pillar-and-lattice gateway with lions on the pillars, not a roofed gatehouse. The order from the street is the gate, the half-moon pond and bridge, then the roofed Dacheng gate, then the hall.
+  - "In a walled court": broadly supported. The hall's court is closed in by the long cloisters, the Dacheng gate and the Chongsheng shrine. An outer wall surrounds the whole complex.
+  - "Double-eaved hip roof": supported by the temple office (重檐廡殿). The Taiwan Tourism Administration says hip-and-gable instead.
+  - Colours: yellow glazed roof, vermilion columns and doors, grey faux-granite surfaces, and muted blue-green Song painting.
+  - Age: the official pages read give no construction years. Non-official sources say 1972–1976, which was not verified.
+- Position: about 1.2 km north-northeast of Taichung Park and 0.76 km northeast of the Yizhong representative point. It is about 1.8–2.0 km north-northeast of the Green River point, Miyahara and Old Taichung Station, and about 2.45 km east of the Science Museum. The Martyrs' Shrine adjoins it.
+- Status: open, free, Tuesday to Sunday 09:00–17:00 and closed Mondays (tourism bureau and temple office).
