+## 17. Second Market / 第二市場 (formal: 臺中市公有第二零售市場)
+
+Verdict: verified for the hexagonal tower and the market's age. "Beside the Green River" is wrong. It is next to the Liuchuan Canal.
+
+- [Taichung Tourism: Second Market (en)](https://travel.taichung.gov.tw/en/attractions/intro/1366): a market about 100 years old at Sanmin Road and Taiwan Boulevard. In the Japanese era it sold high-end goods. A historic hexagonal building marks its centre, and vendors were grouped by trade around a hexagonal layout.
+- [Taichung Tourism: 第二市場 (zh)](https://taichung.travel/zh-tw/attractions/intro/70): formal name 臺中市公有第二零售市場. Hexagonal radial aisles all meet at the central 六角樓, which earned the nickname 六條通. It has over 300 stalls. It is over a century old, was called 新富町市場 in the Japanese era and was nicknamed the Japanese market. The city has repaired it. One photo is captioned 六角樓.
+- [Central District Office: 第二市場及六角樓](https://www.central.taichung.gov.tw/1699766/post): the public market began in 1917. The main structure has three radial wings with a hexagonal main building at the core, and the hexagonal tower dates from 1936.
+- [Taichung Tourism: Second Market nearby attractions](https://travel.taichung.gov.tw/en/attractions/nearbyattractions/1366): the Liuchuan Canal Waterfront is 171 m away. Lyuchuan Canal (the Green River) does not appear in the list, which runs out to 551 m.
+- Official photo of the 六角樓 entrance: a two-storey corner building. The lower floor is red brick with grey wash-stone frames, and a grey lintel carries the name 六角樓 in gold. The upper floor is pale stucco with a shaped, stepped gable parapet and an arched window behind a balcony rail. Other photos show covered aisles with roller-shutter stalls and mural-painted entrances.
+- Address: No. 87, Section 2, Sanmin Road, Central District.
+- Coordinates: latitude `24.14236`, longitude `120.67882`, from the tourism metadata on both language entries, matching the en map link.
+- Plan note check:
+  - "Six-sided tower (六角樓)": supported. The tower dates from 1936. The market itself dates from 1917.
+  - "Over covered market halls": broadly supported. The tower is the hub where the covered radial aisles and three wings meet. It is a two-storey building at the centre of the halls, not a tower standing on their roofs.
+  - "Beside the Green River": wrong. The market is about 170 m east of the Liuchuan Canal (柳川) waterfront, a different canal. The Green River point is about 0.7 km east-southeast. If water appears next to the market, it should be the Liuchuan, or the note should drop the river.
+- Position: about 0.7 km west-southwest of Taichung Park and about 0.7 km northwest of Miyahara. It is about 0.9 km northwest of Old Taichung Station, 0.42 km north of the Prefectural Hall, 1 km southwest of Yizhong and 2.1 km southeast of the Science Museum.
+- Status: operating. The zh tourism page says hours depend on each stall. No official source found records a heritage designation for the tower.
