+**City contract** (`docs/taichung-city-contract.json`). These three maps' entries move with the build:
+- the three districts, Old City North's included;
+- the seven landmarks' doors, footprints, approaches, arrivals and signs;
+- habitats that are exactly the built tall grass, numbered rectangles: `greenway-grass-001`… and `park-grass-001`… (144 in all). The station urban garden is gone under the new lots.
+
+**Encounters.** All park tall grass has a land table at rate 12, Pidgey and Rattata at levels 2–5: Greenway gets one, and Old City's (Taichung Park) moves from levels 2–4 to the same table. Every landmark approach is reachable without entering tall grass.
+
+**Guards.**
+- `check_oldcity_rework.py` proves this build. It records it in `data/taichung/city-rework/oldcity-install.json`: each whole file by digest, and this build's own entries in the eight shared files.
+- `underneath()` hands the frozen guards BASE's files and entries, but only while the tree holds exactly this build. Those guards are check_city_kit, check_old_core, check_cmp (and check_greenway_science through it), check_xitun_final, check_xitun_streets and check_nantun.
+- check_cmp's v8 save profile is re-pinned to this build's commit, for the two Xitun guards' new digests. It reads the build at that commit, so each rebuild that changes the record needs the re-pin again.
+
+**Pending.**
+- validate_city's findings at the seams with Xitun, Nantun North and Wanhe. Those maps are still at today's geometry; they move to the plan in their own increments.
+- For integration:
+  - save v9. The builder writes what it needs to `data/taichung/city-rework/oldcity-save-v9.json`: each map's shift, the events that moved beyond it (Miyahara's door among them), and the 327 Greenway and 474 Old City cells a player can stand on today that the build blocks, each with the nearest reachable open cell that is not tall grass;
