+# Local-player quest-log and Save presentation
+
+The quest-log-only resolver selects complete English/Traditional Chinese sentences by exact original template pointer. It covers13 stock `{PLAYER}` sentences and8 dynamic local-player contexts. Unknown pointers and remote/NPC/rival names retain their identity. Exactly five dynamic local-player setters use the existing `TaichungPlayerTextGet(TAICHUNG_PLAYER_YOU)` API.
+
+Standard contexts: saved game, party switch, item use, PC withdrawal, PC-held-item gift, held-item gift, town departure, home rest, Oak-lab departure, Safari visit, Escape Rope, generic departure and obtained item. Dynamic contexts: multi battle, champion introduction/counter, four wild defeat/catch combinations, and shop sale. Rival slot0 in the champion counter remains the rival; only local slot2 is replaced. The local multi slot0, wild slot5 and sale slot0 likewise remain distinct from every participant/species/location slot.
+
+The additional asm-defined `gText_PlayerSavedTheGame` pointer routes through the existing field resolver to `You saved the game.` / `你儲存了遊戲。`. The asm constant, Save function, global formatter and language controller are unchanged. The field audit now checks this reachable asm template explicitly alongside the prior ten C-defined field templates.
+
+The native recap task/record/replay source restores byte-for-byte to9702950 after reversing only the rendering wrappers/includes and five pointer arguments. Original quest-log text constants, log writers, record sizes, return pointers, identity/trainerID/OT/party storage, Save, font and renderer source are unchanged.
+
+Validation:
+
+```sh
+PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 bash tools/taichung_gameplay/test-quest-log-player-text.sh
+PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 bash tools/taichung_gameplay/test-player-text.sh
+```
+
+The real C helper tests check both locales, all21 original pointers, exact unknown-pointer fallbacks, participant/name/storage sentinels and the existing local YOU getter. The source audit checks every nonlocal placeholder, complete grammatical templates, all actual callsites, immutable storage/replay code and native-font widths with bounded species/item/location/participant values. Templates use at most three lines, at most233px of the236px safe width, and remain inside the recap's256-byte text scan. Remaining stock item/species/outcome names retain their original values; this is not full quest-log localization.
+
+Main must append these **nine** glyphs before native compilation, using the existing append-only Fusion pipeline:
+
+`冠 則 含 商 攜 繩 賣 軍 量`
+
+All nine exist in the pinned font. This branch does not change the codebook/font. The audit preserves the released748-row prefix and permits a same-Fusion append; Main can enforce final coverage with:
+
+```sh
+PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 tools/taichung_gameplay/audit-quest-log-player-text.py --require-glyphs
+```
+
+Native ROM compilation and actual recap/Save confirmation remain Main-owned. No recap suppression, global name replacement, profile, map or Save-data change is included.
