@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@
+# Native badge image upload
+
+Source base: `970295050920093f99a4cc2c4a85d247e0f1afdc`.
+
+The City Pass created all ten sprites successfully, but their icons and locked
+silhouettes were blank in the native runtime. Both collection and award
+templates use `TAG_NONE` and their own ROM `SpriteFrameImage`. Native
+`CreateSpriteAt` reserves OBJ tiles for these images without uploading pixels.
+`BeginAnim` queues the upload only for a frame command. The former
+`gDummySpriteAnimTable` contains only `ANIM_END`, so no copy was requested and
+the scene's cleared OBJ VRAM stayed transparent. Successful sprite allocation
+therefore did not trigger the scene's `?` fallback.
+
+`src/taichung_badges.c` now gives both sizes one shared animation:
+`ANIMCMD_FRAME(0, 1)` followed by `ANIMCMD_END`. Frame zero refers to the single
+image already selected by each template. The first native animation tick queues
+that image; the existing OAM/VBlank lifecycle uploads it. Later ticks remain on
+the same image. Asset bytes, palettes, tags, positions, priority, scene code,
+progress and award logic are unchanged. The small animation arrays are const
+ROM data; there is no new persistent or static RAM.
+
+Verification commands:
+
+```sh
+PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 -B tools/taichung_gameplay/test-native-badge-sprites.py --prove-regression
+bash tools/taichung_gameplay/test-badge-scenes.sh
+```
+
+Both pass. The focused test extracts current native C function bodies and real
+`Sprite`, `OamData` and animation definitions. It executes creation/allocation,
+animation dispatch, image-copy requests, OAM building/loading, and the actual
+City Pass VBlank callback with host memory replacing hardware addresses. All
+ten collection and award payloads match their exact 128/512-byte ROM frames;
+earned and locked palette selections, OAM dimensions/positions, deferred copy
+gating and 120 static frames are checked. The dummy-only negative cases queue
+zero images and leave transparent memory. Reverting only the template's
+animation binding makes the positive copy-queue assertion fail.
+
+Host substitutes are explicit: hardware memcpy/palette transfer, sprite sorting
+(unrelated to image upload and containing documented upstream UB), and unused
+sheet/affine/subsprite branches. The unchanged native dummy callback's unused
+parameter and native frame macro's zero flip initializers require two compiler
+warning exceptions. The existing scene suite still covers bilingual grids,
+awards, navigation/card return and failure cleanup; its asset audit verifies
+the approved PNG/payload/palette hashes and guarded after-win call sites.
+
+This is source and host verification. No ROM build or UI interaction was done
+for this branch; actual native visual confirmation remains Main's next step.
