+Old city west edge rows20–23 and50–53 join Greenway east rows36–39
+and66–69. Greenway west rows24–27 join Xitun east rows56–59. The
+connections work in both directions and use common primary tiles at the seams.
+Other boundary cells are closed. The two old-city roads permit a loop instead
+of requiring the same street on every journey. Running and cycling are enabled
+throughout the exteriors; doors lead to interiors where cycling is disallowed.
+
+The map is a deliberately nonuniform compression. Miyahara remains near the
+station, the park remains north of them, cultural landmarks form a central
+axis, and Fengjia/Maple Garden/the theater form the western cluster. Buildings
+receive enough space for their doors, signs, paths and future artwork. Most
+ordinary city blocks disappear. The original coordinates in the visitor catalog
+remain the source for the real-world map, rather than these game coordinates.
+
+## Landmark door contract
+
+Every exterior door faces south, uses a native animated door with collision1 /
+elevation0, and enters interior warp1. Its southern approach is clear at
+elevation3. Three interior exit tiles (5/6/7,14) all return to the same exterior
+warp; exiting automatically steps the player onto the clear southern approach.
