@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+# Read-only native navigation snapshot, version 1
+
+`gTaichungNavigationBridge` is a separate 48-byte EWRAM packet for the browser minimap. Native is its only writer. It has no requests, acknowledgements, saved fields or visibility preference. The existing `TCLANG01` language protocol remains exactly 32 bytes and unchanged. Browser Minimap On/Off belongs in browser storage.
+
+`src/main.c` calls `TaichungNavigationBridge_Tick(sGameCallbacksRan)` once per main loop after the normal game callbacks, next to the existing language bridge tick. `gameCallbacksRan` describes that loop's actual callback execution, not merely emulator frame advancement. The exact build must publish this symbol's address, version 1, size 48 and magic values in its ROM metadata; consumers must never reuse an address from a different ROM.
+
+## Byte layout
+
+All integers are little-endian. The header is authoritative; do not infer readiness from an address containing plausible coordinates.
+
+| Offset | Type | Meaning |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `00` | u32 | `magicA = 0x414E4354` |
+| `04` | u32 | `magicB = 0x31303056`; combined bytes are `TCNAV001` |
+| `08` | u16 | `version = 1` |
+| `0A` | u16 | `size = 48` |
+| `0C` | u32 | `selfGbaAddress`; must equal the metadata address |
+| `10` | u32 | Publication sequence; nonzero even means complete, odd means being written |
+| `14` | u32 | Frame counter; increments on every tick, including hidden contexts; skips zero |
+| `18` | u32 | Positive flags below |
+| `1C`, `1E` | s16, s16 | Local x/y, zero-based metatiles, or `-1/-1` when invalid |
+| `20`, `21` | u8, u8 | Native map group/number, or `FF/FF` when invalid |
+| `22` | u8 | Facing: 0 unknown, 1 south, 2 north, 3 west, 4 east |
+| `23` | u8 | Native `MAP_TYPE_*`, or 0 when invalid |
+| `24`, `26` | u16, u16 | Current map layout width/height in metatiles; 0 when invalid |
+| `28` | u16 | Hidden-context flags below; nonzero means hide/suspend the live minimap |
+| `2A`, `2C` | u16, u32 | Reserved, always zero in v1 |
+
+The positive flags are `READY=1`, `FIELD=2`, `POSITION_VALID=4`, `OUTDOOR=8`, `INDOOR=16`, `CYCLING=32`, `CAN_TOGGLE_BIKE=64`. `FIELD` means the engine's real main field callback pair; `READY` additionally means its native SaveBlock1 pointer is valid. They do not imply that menus/dialogue are closed. A displayable position also requires `POSITION_VALID` and zero context flags. `CYCLING` reflects native Mach/Acro Bike avatar flags, rather than input or a browser guess. `CAN_TOGGLE_BIKE` comes only from the bike owner's public `TaichungCanToggleBike()` eligibility getter; it means that a fresh secondary-action press in this context can request the native Bike/Get off action. The actual input handler additionally owns its release latch and button priority. Never infer eligibility solely from `OUTDOOR` or `CYCLING`; when bit 6 is absent, use a Back/contextual fallback label.
+
+Hidden-context bits are: callbacks skipped `0001`, not the main field callbacks `0002`, battle `0004`, palette/field transition `0008`, script or locked controls `0010`, dialogue/text printer `0020`, link context `0040`, quest-log replay `0080`, invalid/null save pointer `0100`, invalid/inactive player avatar `0200`, out-of-bounds position/facing `0400`, invalid/unknown map/layout `0800`. New/unknown bits require a conservative hide in v1. Contexts can overlap. Menu tasks that retain the field callback are covered by controls/script/message checks; full-screen selectors and battle callbacks lose `FIELD`.
+
+## Coordinate semantics and map scope
+
+The position comes from `PlayerGetDestCoords`, which reads the actual player's `currentCoords`. The engine includes a seven-metatile border; publication subtracts `MAP_OFFSET` (7) from both axes. Thus `(0,0)` is the upper-left metatile of the current map layout, x increases east, y increases south, and each unit is 16 game pixels. During a tile step, this is the destination tile selected by the native movement engine. There is no pixel interpolation or inferred motion. This matches the mapper's zero-based district and room contracts. The packet includes dimensions for bounds validation.
+
+Connection or warp boundary frames can temporarily put the player outside the current layout. Those frames publish no valid position. Normal walking/cycling within a map publishes every tick. The map IDs come from the current initialized native save location and the dimensions/type from `gMapHeader`; no story, guide-card or exploration state fabricates them.
+
+`OUTDOOR` follows the engine's `IsMapTypeOutdoors`; `INDOOR` covers indoor/underground/secret-base map types. A consumer must map the exact native map pair through the mapper's versioned map-to-world transforms. A mapping for an exterior is not permission to interpret a room's x/y as city coordinates. For an indoor pair, use only an explicitly authored parent-entrance mapping plus an indoor label, or omit the outdoor dot. Unknown map pairs or scopes hide the dot. The full visitor guide remains usable.
+
+## Coherence and freshness
+
+1. Verify metadata belongs to the loaded ROM and the address plus 48 bytes lies wholly in EWRAM (`02000000`–`0203FFFF`). Read `sequence` at `+10`; reject zero or odd values.
+2. Copy all 48 bytes, then reread `sequence`. Require the initial, copied and final sequences to be identical, nonzero and even. Retry on a later poll when publication overlapped the read.
+3. Validate both magic words, exact version/size/self-address, reserved zeros, recognized map scope, required `READY|FIELD|POSITION_VALID` flags, zero context flags, facing 1–4, nonzero dimensions and `0 <= x < width`, `0 <= y < height`.
+4. Require `frameCounter` to advance for this emulator instance before treating a newly attached/reset snapshot as live. Track the last observed advancement with a monotonic browser clock. A suggested stale threshold is one second without advancement while the emulator is expected to run; hide/suspend immediately for any invalid context or when the emulator is deliberately paused/loading.
+5. A static coordinate while the frame counter advances is a stationary player, not stale data. A frozen frame counter is not live tracking. Wrap/reset is a new freshness epoch: discard cached locations, wait for another coherent advancing sample, and revalidate the loaded ROM metadata. Do not extrapolate, animate or retain a dot labeled live from a rejected snapshot.
+
+No snapshot is guaranteed fresh merely because its sequence is even. Emulator snapshots can restore old packet bytes; pause/reset/import/ROM replacement must reset the browser's freshness history. This is presentation data, not an authoritative gameplay save or a browser memory-write interface.
+
+## Delivery and validation scope
+
+This source slice provides the packet, tick implementation and main-loop hookup. Exact symbol-address metadata, browser integration and map transforms belong to their existing owners. Actual feature-ROM walking/cycling/door/menu checks are recorded in `taichung-navigation-bike-qa.md`; canonical integration must repeat them against matching metadata. It adds exactly 48 static EWRAM bytes; publication uses a temporary stack snapshot and no persistent map cache. Language data and native save variables are not read or written by this module, apart from reading the current map location through a validated SaveBlock1 pointer.
+
+`python3 tools/taichung_gameplay/test-navigation-bridge.py` compiles the actual publisher with strict host warnings and bounded native API mocks. It passes layout/offset checks, map-local coordinates and bounds, indoor/outdoor scope, cycling and the shared bike-eligibility getter, every hidden-context category, null/invalid save/avatar/map state, stationary frame updates, reserved zeros and nonzero sequence/frame wrap. This host check does not run the ROM or verify the shared frame hook, browser memory reads or mapper transforms.
