+## Challenge and reward
+
+Talking to Lian checks only Park completion, presents the authored greeting,
+then offers Yes/No. No/B returns without party preparation or progress. Yes
+uses the existing preparation adapter: level 50, full recovery, unchanged
+held-item/mail handling. Wild and sight preferences do not block this voluntary
+challenge. City battles keep the existing no-experience/no-EV-gain rules.
+
+Only the matching prepared/started native battle's actual win writes bit 1.
+The Park script and C feedback also require the won result plus Park's own
+recorded bit before showing earned-badge text. Defeat, decline, skipped trainer
+flags and non-wins do not award it. Repeated completed interaction shows the
+recorded-badge message, without another fight or reward. No rematch is enabled.
+Quest-log playback exits before preparation and `trainerbattle`, preventing
+the native replay shortcut from fabricating a fought flag or leaving tracking
+armed without a battle.
+
+## Loss notice lifetime
+
+A genuine matching `B_OUTCOME_LOST` records one volatile notice for that gym.
+The ordinary whiteout/heal path, Station checkpoint, walking between maps and
+leaving/reentering Park preserve it. The first later voluntary Park-host
+interaction shows the loss line once, consumes it, then greets/offers a retry.
+Declining that retry leaves no notice to show on the next visit. No new saved
+variable or automatic field dialogue is introduced.
+
+Wrong halls neither consume nor display Park's notice during ordinary
+interaction/decline. A newly accepted valid challenge or explicit challenge
+cancellation clears the stale notice; raw generic non-win results cannot
+create it. Duplicate callbacks cannot fabricate a notice. New Game and every
+native Continue helper entry explicitly cancel transient tracking before any
+save-version/empty-party early return, including quest-log SRAM reload paths.
+An ordinary native Save does not serialize the notice; fresh Continue clears
+it. Emulator snapshots can intentionally restore EWRAM and are outside this
+native SRAM contract.
+
+## Delivery gates
+
+Before Main integrates, record a clean source checkpoint and exact isolated
+ROM hash, reviewed Lian art/text bindings, appended glyph compatibility, both
+languages, decline, genuine loss and recovery, one-time retry notice, genuine
+win preserving Jun's bit, repeat interaction, team-item preservation and native
+Save followed by fresh-import Continue. The released presentation and its
+presenter save remain the stable fallback throughout.
