+# Level 50 team presets
+
+The native Team picker supports the contiguous Kanto species constants #001–150, Bulbasaur through Mewtwo. Mew and later-generation species are outside this first roster. `TAICHUNG_TEAM_LEVEL` is 50. The caller creates or normalizes the Pokemon; this module never changes its level, species, identity, held item, stats, HP, status, party slot, language, preferences or badge progress.
+
+`TaichungTeamSpeciesAllowed(species)` checks the roster. `TaichungTeamGetPresetMoves(species)` returns four slots, or `NULL` for an unsupported species. `TaichungTeamApplyPreset(mon)` installs those moves, resets PP Ups and restores each move's base PP through `SetMonMoveSlot`. Unsupported species and a null pointer are left untouched. Empty slots use `MOVE_NONE` and zero PP.
+
+The authored source is `data/taichung/team-presets/curated.tsv`: each of the 150 species has four explicit slots and a design rationale. `generate-team-presets.py` emits `src/data/taichung_team_presets.h` and the readable `profiles.json`; `--check` rejects drift. Each set uses native FireRed level-up moves at any natural level, level-up moves retained from a pre-evolution, or that species' native TM/HM/tutor compatibility. The game grants them directly; obtaining a TM, meeting a tutor, trading, leveling or evolving is not required. The direct evolved-form picker can intentionally create forms such as Dragonite at level 50. No preset depends on Return/Frustration friendship scaling, Hidden Power IV tuning, an egg move, event move, held item or an imported later-generation move.
+
+Useful coverage and straightforward attacks are preferred to competitive optimization. FireRed's type-based physical/special rules still apply. Some species are intrinsically weak and equal levels do not equalize their stats. Sleep, status, setup and recovery moves are deliberate options; this is an initial balance pass. No self-KO or OHKO moves appear in these sets. Manual move editing is separate work.
+
+Six species honestly have fewer than four moves:
+
+| Species | Preset |
+| --- | --- |
+| Caterpie | Tackle, String Shot |
+| Metapod | Tackle, String Shot, Harden |
+| Weedle | Poison Sting, String Shot |
+| Kakuna | Poison Sting, String Shot, Harden |
+| Magikarp | Tackle, Flail, Splash |
+| Ditto | Transform |
+
+Metapod and Kakuna keep their legal pre-evolution attacks so they can act immediately. Ditto uses its native transformation behavior rather than invented attacks.
+
+Run `python3 tools/taichung_gameplay/validate-team-presets.py` in the native checkout. It parses the real species constants, learnsets, evolution links, TM/HM and FireRed tutor tables, and battle move PP/power. The initial pass covers all 150 entries and 590 nonempty move slots; it checks roster completeness, duplicates, packed empty slots, positive PP, legal move sources and a damaging move for every species except Ditto. Source counts, preferring level inheritance when a move has several sources: 370 level/inherited slots, 178 TM/HM slots and 42 tutor slots. The validator also rejects identical direct-evolution sets, unsupported Solar Beam and Dream Eater combinations, and disagreement with the authored profiles. `--audit-json PATH` exports every move and its verified source. This source-data validation does not substitute for the caller's ROM build and native picker/battle runtime checks.
+
+
+## Intentional species roles
+
+The battle level stays 50, but the no-grinding picker directly grants late natural
+moves such as Dragonite's Outrage and Rhydon's Megahorn. This is deliberate and
+uses the engine's actual Gen III data, not moves invented from newer games.
+Every evolution differs; the full rationale for every species is in profiles.json.
+
+| Family / example | Role and upgrade |
+| --- | --- |
+| Bulbasaur → Ivysaur → Venusaur | Seed-and-recovery support → poison coverage and Growth → Solar Beam with Sunny Day, Sleep Powder and Sludge Bomb |
+| Charmander → Charmeleon → Charizard | Metal Claw and Dragon Rage → Slash and Dragon Claw → Flamethrower, Fly, Dragon Claw and Earthquake |
+| Squirtle → Wartortle → Blastoise | Simple Water Pulse and utility → reliable Surf and Ice Beam → Hydro Pump burst plus reliable Surf and broad coverage |
+| Pikachu → Raichu | Quick Attack and Iron Tail → Brick Break and team Light Screen support |
+| Arcanine | Flamethrower and Extreme Speed: recognizable speed and reliable fire damage |
+| Machamp | Cross Chop, Rock Slide and Earthquake, supported by Bulk Up |
+| Gengar / Hypno | Hypnosis enables Dream Eater; Gengar retains Shadow Ball for its identity, with special Thunderbolt and Dream Eater doing the special damage |
+| Flareon | Overheat's special-attack drop leaves Body Slam, Shadow Ball and Quick Attack unaffected |
+| Rhydon | Physical Earthquake, Rock Slide and Megahorn with Swords Dance |
+| Dragonite | Outrage, Fly, Earthquake and Agility; Gen III Dragon attacks are special, so no misleading physical-only boost |
+
+## Existing teams and the entry reminder
+
+Opening Team, entering a gym, or starting a Taichung battle compares the existing
+party's four moves with the curated preset. A changed set is refreshed once,
+including base PP; unchanged sets keep their remaining PP. Move-only refresh does
+not heal HP/status or change identity, items, EXP, badges, saves or position. Eggs,
+unsupported species, non-city maps and active battles are excluded. Authored gym
+trainer moves are still preserved by the native custom-moveset flag.
+
+Each of the ten unbeaten gym rooms prompts a one-member team once per actual map
+entry, in native bilingual dialogue: Choose team / Not now. Team returns to the
+same room and resumes the script. B also declines. Two or more members, already
+completed gyms and non-gym halls do not prompt. The visit flag is a temporary
+native map variable; there is no new saved state or forced team size. Leaders
+remain three Pokémon for short visits, as the user chose.
