+# Xitun rework (phase 2b, with the 2026-11-09 fill pass and raised highway)
+
+Xitun is built natively on `claude/xitun-rework` as the 45×69 map at world (−5, −5). Rebuild it with `tools/taichung/kit/install_xitun.py`; never hand-edit `map.bin`. `tools/taichung/kit/check_xitun_rework.py` proves the result. Its `underneath()` lets the older Xitun guards check the state from before the rework.
+
+The map comes from two inputs:
+
+- today's Xitun at 3634df4 (claude/city-rework: the live v9 source with the Maple Garden's registered collision, and city-kit 842e9da), for the landmark art, the signs and the kit;
+- `data/taichung/xitun-rework/fill.json`. This holds the coordinator's `artifacts/city-rework/plan-cells.txt` for Xitun's rect, one character per cell, with that file's sha256. It also holds the building on each of the plan's lots.
+
+To preview without touching the tree, run:
+
+```sh
+python3 tools/taichung/kit/draft_xitun.py OUT_DIR --rev 3634df4
+```
+
+It writes `xitun.png` (16 px per tile, world coordinates), `xitun-labelled.png`, `xitun-draft.bin` and `xitun-draft.json`. The JSON holds the reachability report, the seam rows and columns, the strip check and the newly blocked cells.
+
+## Size and coordinates
+
+- **Plan rect:** (−5, −5) to (40, 64), so the map is 45×69. Local = world + 5.
+- **Map buffer:** (45 + 15) × (69 + 14) = 4,980 cells, under the 10,240 limit.
+- **Save v9:** positions shift by (+5, +5). `data/taichung/xitun-rework/install.json` lists, under `newlyBlocked` (today's coordinates), the 396 cells that are walkable today and blocked now. Most are the new building lots and trees on what was open paving.
+
+## What the plan sets
+
+- **Highway, 6 lanes.** World columns −5…0 and rows −5…0, in the kit's `hw-ns-0…5` and `hw-ew-0…5`. At the north-west corner the north highway crosses over the west one (`hw-ew-5-parapet`, with `hw-ns-N-under-n` on row 1).
+- **Retaining wall** on the highway's city side, solid: the north face (`wall-n-upper` on row 1, `wall-n-lower` on row 2) from x 2, and the west wall's top (`wall-w-top`) on column 1 from row 1, so it runs up to the highway at the inner corner, with its shadow on the planted bank (`wall-w-bank`) on column 2 from row 3.
+- **Streets.** These are in kit pieces, each with the 5-cell profile (sidewalk, three asphalt, sidewalk):
+  - S1 runs on asphalt rows 16–18 and S2 on rows 48–50, from x 4 to the Greenway seam. At x 3 each stops at a kerb against the west wall: the sidewalk wraps across the end, with `st-bollards-e` on the three asphalt rows.
+  - X26 runs on asphalt columns 26–28, from S1 to the Nantun North seam.
+  - Crosswalks sit at x 25 and 29, and on rows 47 and 51.
+- **Landmarks** keep today's art on the plan's landmark cells:
+  - Fengjia, x 18–29, y 8–14;
+  - the Maple Garden pond, x 10–19, y 27–33;
+  - the Theater, x 3–20, y 37–45.
+
+  The three doors, (24, 12), (12, 32) and (12, 44), do not move.
+- **Maple Garden park** covers x 3–24, y 24–36:
+  - a ring of 2×2 trees;
+  - 99 cells of tall grass;
+  - a 2-wide paver path on rows 34–35, from X26's sidewalk to the pond's doorstep at (12, 33), with a stub at x 23–24 on row 36.
+- **Fill.** Every other cell takes one fixed piece for its plan class:
+  - city paving `0x16E`;
+  - path `0x175`;
+  - short grass `0x001`;
+  - tall grass `0x00D`;
+  - hedge `0x005`;
+  - tree `0x00E/0x00F/0x016/0x017`.
+
+  Trees stand only where the plan puts them. No trees are scattered on paving.
+- **Buildings.** 36 buildings fill all 698 lot cells, one building per lot, except that a 6-row lot takes two 3-row stalls. The art is today's stall, kiosk or Shen Ji home, stretched to the lot's width by repeating the middle columns. A 4-row stall doubles its roof row.
+  - The three kinds alternate across the district; each takes its lot's size.
+  - None of the buildings has a door.
+- **Signs.**
+  - Fengjia's sign stays at (21, 14) and the Theater's at (9, 46), on the plan's paving.
+  - Maple Garden's old cell, (9, 34), is now tall grass. Its sign moves to (24, 33), the short grass where the path meets X26's sidewalk. This is the only event that moves beyond the shift.
+- **Connections:** Greenway (right) and Nantun North (down) both have offset 0.
+
+## Seams
+
+- **Greenway (east, world x 39 | 40).** Xitun's column 39 is open on rows 6, 11, 15–51 and 56–63, where the plan has paving or street; the building lots close the rest. On Greenway's side, G41's west sidewalk on column 40 is open along its whole length.
+- **Nantun North (south, world y 63 | 64).** Columns 23–29 are open: X26 and the paving beside it. Columns 38–39 are also open, at the foot of G41's sidewalk. The tree line closes x 3–22 and 30–37, and North puts a hedge along its row 64 below them.
+- **Seam strips.** Greenway draws Xitun's last 7 columns (world 33–39) with its own tilesets, and Nantun North draws Xitun's last 7 rows (world 57–63) with its own. Those strips therefore hold primary and kit pieces only, so no Shen Ji home stands there. The plan's homes in the strips are kiosks or stalls instead. `draft_xitun.py` and the guard check both strips on every run.
+
+## Tall grass and encounters
+
+The park's tall grass is Xitun's only encounter grass. It is four contract habitats:
+
+- `maple-garden-park-north`, world (5, 26)–(22, 26);
+- `maple-garden-park-west`, (5, 27)–(9, 36);
+- `maple-garden-park-east`, (20, 27)–(22, 33);
+- `maple-garden-park-south`, (10, 36)–(19, 36).
+
+They share one land table: rate 12, Pidgey and Rattata, levels 2–5. Today's Fengjia pocket garden is now building lots, so its habitat is gone.
+
+## Open
+
+- **Save v9 migration, heal and fly spots, the minimap contract, the landing map and the city guide exports:** the coordinator.
+- **Names:** the highways stay unnamed until the landmark-sources check.
