+
+- **Roads.** Fengjia Road runs east–west at y16–18 and Theater Road at y48–50. Xitun Road runs north–south at x26–28, from y16 to the promenade at y56; pavers carry on to the south edge. Lane lines, crosswalks and paved sidewalks come from Codex's city-v3 road templates, without the speckle texture and drawn in the existing Fengjia palette 9.
+- **Homes.** Eleven Shen Ji small homes from Codex's city-v3 object library (`890b0ca`) are placed: an east block, the north-east corner and a south row. Their foreground art uses palette 12, which v7 left unused, over the existing pavers.
+- **Existing props.** Market stalls, glass kiosks, street trees, tree lines, flower beds and shrubs reuse Xitun primary art at its existing IDs. The south neighborhood's second row is market stalls.
+- **Highway edges.** The world's west and north edges are highway, not tree walls. The west one is the shared edge kit (`tools/taichung/nantun/edge_art.py`, byte-identical to the Nantun branch) down x0–2, so it continues into Nantun North's highway. The north one is the same carriageway turned east–west along y0–2, drawn in Xitun's bank: westbound lanes north of the median and eastbound south. Both are solid. Shrubs close the trees the highway cuts in half. The highway is unnamed: no source places a named road on these edges yet.
+- **Seam promenade.** The released paver promenade at y56–59 still leads from the end of Xitun Road to the Greenway seam.
+- **Nantun North seam.** The south tree wall opens at x26–29 on rows 62–63 into pavers (word `0x3175`), exactly as `claude/nantun-skeleton` writes them, so the pavers below Xitun Road reach Nantun North. The connection entry in Xitun's `map.json` comes from the Nantun branch, not from this one.
+
+## Tileset bank
+
+Released definitions, graphics and palettes 0–11 are byte-identical. The released bank defines 351 secondary metatiles, 64 of them empty (all-zero words and attribute) and unreferenced by the map, scripts, door tables and Greenway. The 25 new definitions fill those empty slots: 5 road surfaces, 15 home cells and 5 north-highway cells. 39 empty slots remain.
+
+Xitun's own graphics append after the 288 released tiles (62 new, up to tile 349). The edge kit then takes its reserved slots: definitions `0x3E0`–`0x3E6` after one empty slot, and graphics 352–373 (`0x3E0`–`0x3F5`). Any district that installs the kit there renders a donated highway strip identically. Nothing references the door-animation tiles 1016–1023.
+
+## Seams
+
+Neighbours draw the Xitun cells they can see with their own banks.
+
+- **Greenway** sees x33–39 from row 25 down. Those cells hold only primary art, and every visible cell renders identically in both banks, in both directions (585 cells).
+- **Nantun North** connects below Xitun on `claude/nantun-skeleton` and sees rows 57–63 through `gTileset_TaichungGreenwayPrivate` and its own bank. Those 280 cells hold only primary art that renders identically in that primary, or the edge kit. The road surface and homes therefore stop above row 57. The guard also keeps the eight seam cells open as those pavers.
+
+The Fengjia, Maple Garden and Theater art, the Theater block at x4–19/y35–44, the three doors, their approaches and arrivals, and the signs all keep their exact words.
+
+## Walking and save version 8
+
+353 formerly valid positions become solid (the highway's x2 path and row-2 cells, homes, stalls, kiosks and trees), and 148 formerly solid cells open, including the eight Nantun seam cells. All 1,367 final valid positions connect to the Fengjia arrival, and validate_city still pairs every landmark room and seam.
+
+Save version 8 is drafted for Main's review. On Continue it refreshes a saved Xitun map cache from every older version. A saved position or pending target on a newly solid cell moves to its nearest open cell: Manhattan distance first, then south, west, east, north. Door warps never become targets, and neither do tall grass cells. The v8 repair runs after the v4 and v7 Xitun repairs. Five old v4 Theater targets that now sit under street trees therefore chain into their v8 rows. Door warps, other districts and v8 or newer saves are untouched.
+
+## Files
+
+- `tools/taichung/streetscape/xitun_streets_layout.py` writes `data/taichung/xitun-streets/ground.txt` and `objects.json`.
+- `tools/taichung/streetscape/xitun_streets.py` copies the pinned Shen Ji home into `kit.json` (`kit`), writes the bank and `bank.json` (`bank`), writes the map (`map`) and prints the C repair table (`save-table`). Every output is rebuilt from `a72bd0e`, so reruns are byte-identical.
+- `tools/taichung/nantun/edge_art.py` is the shared edge kit, unchanged from the Nantun branch.
+- `tools/taichung/streetscape/check_xitun_streets.py` is the guard. It rebuilds the bank and map from the pinned inputs and requires byte equality. It also checks the released and empty slots, the edge kit against the shared kit, the highway edges, both seams, the native walking geometry, the repair table against the actual map delta, the version gates and the host test data, and rejects 25 corruptions.
+- `check_xitun_final.py` checks the frozen v7 scene underneath and delegates the five street files to the guard. `check_cmp.py` binds the exact v8 save pair and geometry in a separate child commit.
+
+```
+python3 -B tools/taichung/streetscape/check_xitun_streets.py --self-test
+python3 -B tools/taichung/landmarks/check_xitun_final.py --self-test
+python3 -B tools/taichung/landmarks/check_cmp.py --self-test
+python3 -B tools/taichung/validate_city.py
+bash tools/taichung_gameplay/test-save.sh
+```
+
+Runtime acceptance is separate: walking and cycling, door round trips, the Greenway seam, the highway edges, blocking, Save/Reset/Continue and real old-save migrations on the exact ROM. Main owns save versions and integration. The Miyahara street and OldCity building proposals also draft a version 8, so Main has to sequence them. On `claude/nantun-skeleton`, Nantun North's held rows 0–3 at x0–2 can now become the edge kit, and its opening at Xitun x26–29, y62–63 is already authored here, so both branches write the same Xitun `map.bin`.
